Audit these NEW results for overclaims and defects. Provide concise final review (maximum 700 words), not implementation, payloads, concealment/evasion changes, key extraction or challenge solutions. You previously gave a generic review: that was not independent verification. Now inspect the actual verification harness and exact tool outcomes. The frozen wrapper feeds all six core inputs directly; BUSY/LED are direct core outputs; only MISO has an XOR output mask. A constant-zero abstract core exposes any mask event. The proposed compositional claim is mask-free behavior under two specified well-formed normal transactions, combined with unchanged-core input coupling. It is NOT a proof that the underlying cipher is cryptographically correct, a proof for arbitrary protocol traces, or an unbounded proof over indefinitely many operations. Need assess whether assume/clock/reset/sampling semantics support the scoped claim. Yosys uses async2sync and 161 SAT steps. A negative control drops only the normal-word exclusions and finds a counterexample. No design was changed. Review boundedness and what extra checks are needed; do not equate a named cipher with architectural recovery.

